MAKUENI WEST DIOCESE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
Comprehensive Module Specification Document

TABLE OF CONTENTS
1.Authentication & User Access
2.System Setup & Configuration (Super Admin)
3.Diocese Portal Modules
4.Regional Portal Modules
5.Subregion Portal Modules
6.Church Portal Modules
7.Shared Modules (Cross-Level Access)

1. AUTHENTICATION & USER ACCESS

Login (/auth/login)
Purpose: Secure authentication for all organizational levels
Contents:
Email or phone number input field
Password input with show/hide toggle
Role-based automatic redirection after successful login
"Remember me" checkbox for persistent sessions
"Forgot password" link
Multi-factor authentication (SMS OTP) for sensitive roles
Login attempt tracking and account lockout after failed attempts
Session timeout settings
Last login timestamp display
Device fingerprinting for security
Support for multiple active sessions across devices

User Registration (/auth/register)
Purpose: New user account creation with approval workflow
Contents:
Personal information form (full name, phone, email, ID number)
Organization selection dropdown (Diocese/Region/Subregion/Church)
Specific organization selection based on type
Role request selection (Pastor, Council Member, Overseer, etc.)
Password creation with strength indicator
Password confirmation field
Email verification via OTP
Phone verification via SMS OTP
Terms and conditions acceptance checkbox
Data privacy policy acknowledgment
Profile photo upload (optional)
Pending approval notification
Admin notification for approval queue
Registration confirmation email/SMS

Password Reset (/auth/password-reset)
Purpose: Secure password recovery process
Contents:
Email or phone number input for account identification
Identity verification via OTP
OTP delivery method selection (SMS/Email)
OTP input field with resend option
OTP expiration timer (10 minutes)
New password creation field
Password strength requirements display
Password confirmation field
Security question verification (optional)
Success notification with auto-redirect to login
Password reset confirmation email/SMS

Two-Factor Authentication Setup (/auth/2fa-setup)
Purpose: Enhanced security for user accounts
Contents:
2FA activation toggle
Authentication method selection (SMS/Email/Authenticator App)
Phone number verification for SMS
QR code generation for authenticator apps
Backup codes generation and download
Test 2FA functionality before activation
2FA status indicator
Trusted devices management
2FA deactivation process with identity verification

Session Management (/auth/sessions)
Purpose: Manage active user sessions across devices
Contents:
List of active sessions with device information
Last activity timestamp per session
IP address and location per session
Browser/device type identification
Current session indicator
Terminate session functionality
"Logout all other devices" option
Session history log (last 30 days)
Suspicious activity alerts

2. SYSTEM SETUP & CONFIGURATION
(Super Admin / Diocese Council Only)

Initial Diocese Setup (/setup/diocese/initial)
Purpose: First-time diocese system configuration
Contents:
Diocese official name
Diocese acronym/short name
Bishop information (name, contact, photo)
Diocese establishment date
Diocese headquarters address
Physical location coordinates (for mapping)
Diocese phone numbers (office, emergency)
Diocese email addresses (official, support)
Diocese website URL
Diocese logo upload (multiple sizes)
Diocese letterhead template upload
Diocese motto/vision statement
Diocese mission statement
Primary contact person details
Timezone selection
Primary currency selection
Secondary currencies (if applicable)
Fiscal year start month
Language preferences
Date format preferences (DD/MM/YYYY or MM/DD/YYYY)

Region Management (/setup/regions)
Purpose: Create and manage regional divisions
Contents:
Add new region button
Region creation form: 
oRegion name
oRegion code/identifier
oGeographic coverage description
oHas subregions flag (YES/NO)
oRegional overseer assignment (searchable dropdown)
oRegional overseer contact details
oRegion office address (if applicable)
oRegion phone number
oRegion email address
oRegion establishment date
oRegion status (Active/Inactive)
List of all regions (table view): 
oRegion name and code
oRegional overseer name
oNumber of subregions (if applicable)
oNumber of churches under region
oTotal members in region
oRegion status
oAction buttons (View/Edit/Delete)
Region details view: 
oFull region information
oSubregions list (if has_subregions = TRUE)
oChurches list (if has_subregions = FALSE)
oRegion statistics dashboard
oRegion performance metrics
Edit region functionality
Delete region (with confirmation and validation)
Bulk region import from CSV/Excel
Region export functionality
Region hierarchy visualization (tree view)

Subregion Management (/setup/subregions)
Purpose: Create and manage subregional divisions
Contents:
Filter by region dropdown
Add new subregion button
Subregion creation form: 
oParent region selection (dropdown)
oSubregion name
oSubregion code/identifier
oGeographic coverage description
oSubregion overseer assignment
oSubregion overseer contact details
oSubregion office address (if applicable)
oSubregion phone number
oSubregion email address
oSubregion establishment date
oSubregion status (Active/Inactive)
List of all subregions (table view): 
oSubregion name and code
oParent region name
oSubregion overseer name
oNumber of churches
oTotal members
oStatus
oAction buttons (View/Edit/Delete)
Subregion details view: 
oFull subregion information
oChurches under this subregion
oSubregion statistics
oPerformance metrics
Edit subregion functionality
Delete subregion (with validation)
Transfer subregion to different region
Bulk subregion import
Subregion export functionality

Church Registration (/setup/churches)
Purpose: Register and manage all churches in diocese
Contents:
Add new church button
Church registration form: 
oChurch full name
oChurch acronym/short name
oChurch code/identifier (auto-generated or manual)
oRegion selection (dropdown)
oSubregion selection (conditional - only if region has subregions)
oParent organization determination (automatic based on structure)
oPastor assignment (searchable dropdown of pastors)
oPastor contact details
oChurch physical address
oChurch GPS coordinates (for mapping)
oChurch phone numbers
oChurch email address
oChurch establishment date
oChurch registration date in diocese
oChurch building ownership status (Owned/Rented/Borrowed)
oChurch capacity (seating)
oChurch status (Active/Inactive/Under Construction)
oService times configuration: 
Sunday service times (multiple services)
Midweek service times
Prayer meeting times
Other regular services
List of all churches (table/grid view): 
oChurch name and code
oRegion and subregion (if applicable)
oPastor name
oTotal members
oChurch status
oTithe compliance status
oLast report submitted date
oAction buttons (View/Edit/Delete/Transfer)
Church details view: 
oFull church information
oDemographics summary
oFinancial summary
oRecent activities
oCompliance status
oPerformance metrics
Edit church functionality
Transfer church to different subregion/region
Church status management (activate/deactivate)
Bulk church import from CSV/Excel
Church export functionality
Church location map view (all churches plotted)
Church search and advanced filtering: 
oBy region/subregion
oBy pastor name
oBy establishment date
oBy status
oBy compliance status

